1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,700
See you later, Origami.

2
00:00:02,780 --> 00:00:03,540
Yeah, later.

3
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:14,780
Mom and Dad.

4
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:15,780
Oh, no.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,980
Mom and Dad.

6
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:42,760
What happened?

7
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:55,620
It's your fault.

8
00:00:56,260 --> 00:00:56,580
You!

9
00:00:57,900 --> 00:00:59,660
I won't forgive you!

10
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:00,800
Ever!

11
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:02,820
I'm gonna kill you!

12
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:04,060
I swear!

13
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:05,820
Someday, I will!

14
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:27,900
Good morning, little bed buddy.

15
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:28,620
Ah!

16
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:29,140
Ah!

17
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:29,660
Ah!

18
00:01:29,660 --> 00:01:30,040
Ah!

19
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:30,260
Ah!

20
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:30,680
Ah!

21
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:30,700
Ah!

22
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:31,100
Ah!

23
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:39,940
Sharing a bed is so dreamy.

24
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:41,680
All the romance and sweetness.

25
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:44,040
If only it could last beyond the morning.

26
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:45,900
What a paradise life would be.

27
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:46,900
Is there a favor?

28
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:47,400
Itusta no building.

29
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:58,240
Very sweet.

30
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:28,220
See you next time.

31
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:58,220
See you next time.

32
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:28,220
See you next time.

33
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:29,960
No, I'm not!

34
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,800
And how were you able to transform anyway?

35
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:33,780
Right, I never told you about that.

36
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:35,360
The deal with Natsumi, I mean.

37
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:36,020
What?

38
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:38,100
Wait, was the seal incomplete or something?

39
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:38,940
Oh, no.

40
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:41,200
The seal itself was actually successful.

41
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:45,380
So, are the transformations triggered by her emotions then?

42
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:48,280
Yeah, I guess that's one way of putting it.

43
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:51,580
She's not the most stable in case you haven't picked that up.

44
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,140
No fair.

45
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:55,580
What are you two whispering about over there?

46
00:03:55,940 --> 00:03:58,420
Fear of missing out has always been kind of a thing with me.

47
00:03:58,840 --> 00:03:59,900
Just look at her.

48
00:04:00,060 --> 00:04:03,100
You gotta do something about transforming over every little thing.

49
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:06,900
Listen, I totally get that you're jealous that Shido fell for me.

50
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:11,360
But it's not my fault your body is so inferior to my voluptuous one.

51
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:13,820
It's not my fault I'm a munchkin!

52
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:15,720
I happen to be having a growth spurt!

53
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:19,000
You're the cutest!

54
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:20,780
Stop laughing immediately!

55
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:22,180
Look at your red little face!

56
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:23,340
Shut up, you horny!

57
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:28,240
Origami still hasn't shown up.

58
00:04:31,540 --> 00:04:34,580
That was obviously one of DEM's CR units.

59
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:37,140
So, what does this mean?

60
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,420
I don't get it.

61
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:40,480
Where is she?

62
00:04:42,860 --> 00:04:43,460
Stand!

63
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:44,840
Bow!

64
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:46,180
Sit!

65
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:50,200
Um, before I take attendance,

66
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:53,300
I'm afraid I have a rather sad announcement to make, everyone.

67
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:53,940
Whoa.

68
00:04:54,140 --> 00:04:55,080
What's up, Temmy girl?

69
00:04:55,280 --> 00:04:56,980
Did the matchmaking not work out?

70
00:04:57,220 --> 00:04:57,660
Oh, snap!

71
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:58,360
Are you catfish?

72
00:04:58,640 --> 00:04:59,980
That is so lame!

73
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:00,800
Ahem.

74
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:02,580
No, actually.

75
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:05,900
Origami Tobiichi will be transferring to another school

76
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:07,660
due to unexpected circumstances.

77
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:09,360
Transferring?

78
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:11,280
Transfer?

79
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:12,840
Hold on, back up.

80
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:13,800
What do you mean?

81
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:15,360
What exactly is going on?

82
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:18,780
Unfortunately, I don't really have any other details.

83
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:22,920
I got a call from her out of the blue and all she said was that she was transferring.

84
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:25,520
She said she'd send in the forms later on.

85
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:26,940
No!

86
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:29,020
Did she say what school she's going to?

87
00:05:29,020 --> 00:05:31,120
Oh, well, she sort of did.

88
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:33,380
She said something about a school in England.

89
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:34,060
England?

90
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:35,520
I see.

91
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:41,100
You okay, Itsuka?

92
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:43,040
Um, it's just...

93
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:43,760
my stomach!

94
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:45,900
Yeah, it's been really hurting me today.

95
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:46,500
She...

96
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:47,500
You stay where you are!

97
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:48,500
I'll be fine!

98
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:49,000
I'll be fine!

99
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:49,500
Ah!

100
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:50,000
Ah!

101
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:50,500
Ah!

102
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:51,000
Ah!

103
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:52,500
Ah!

104
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:53,000
Ah!

105
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,900
Why do I have to be the way that I am?

106
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:57,460
Um, here I finally got up early enough.

107
00:05:57,460 --> 00:06:01,800
I never meant to wake him up while I was in that form.

108
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:09,580
Thanks a lot for the tea, Natsumi!

109
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:10,580
Me?

110
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:11,580
Sure, no sweat.

111
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:13,580
So is there something you need from me?

112
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:14,580
Oh, um...

113
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:15,580
Funny you ask.

114
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:19,580
What could possibly bring this one to my room?

115
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:20,580
I can't even guess.

116
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:24,580
Oh, I know.

117
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:27,580
I bet she bears some kind of grudge and came to get revenge!

118
00:06:27,580 --> 00:06:34,580
The truth is, I was thinking that since you just moved in, you probably don't know the city all that well and you might like some hope.

119
00:06:34,580 --> 00:06:35,580
That's right!

120
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:36,580
That has to be it!

121
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:40,580
After all, I was fooling Shido by impersonating her little friend!

122
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:43,580
I mean, it's not like I know all there is to know either!

123
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:46,580
So I actually may not be all that helpful to you.

124
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:49,580
She waited until all the others were gone to make her move!

125
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:54,580
But if you're interested, I would be more than happy to show you around the city!

126
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:55,580
Huh?

127
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:58,580
It's just that I've always spent this time of day all by myself.

128
00:06:58,580 --> 00:07:04,580
But since you're here now, well, I was hoping that you and I could spend some time hanging out together.

129
00:07:04,580 --> 00:07:08,580
Because... well, just because... we're friends, aren't we?

130
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:11,580
Whoa! I've gotta marry this girl!

131
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:16,580
Hey, if you're willing to show me around the city, then heck yeah, I'll take you up on it!

132
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:18,580
When do we leave? Let's go already!

133
00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:22,580
I'm sorry. The number you've dialed is out of the service area.

134
00:07:22,580 --> 00:07:24,580
Please hang up and try again.

135
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:26,580
Why isn't she picking up?

136
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:29,580
Hope you're here, Origami.

137
00:07:33,580 --> 00:07:35,580
Okay, I've made it inside.

138
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:48,580
Origami! It's me! Say something if you're there!

139
00:07:56,580 --> 00:07:58,580
It's open!

140
00:07:58,580 --> 00:07:59,580
Origami!

141
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:06,580
Where in the world did you run off to? And for what?

142
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:16,580
Your lunch looks so yummy, Coterie!

143
00:08:16,580 --> 00:08:18,580
Plunk, thanks. My brother made it for me.

144
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:19,580
Now let's eat!

145
00:08:19,580 --> 00:08:25,580
What do you mean you can't find Shido? He's in class, isn't he?

146
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:29,580
It seems he skipped out as soon as he heard about Origami transferring schools.

147
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:35,580
Well, that's weird. Doesn't that timing seem suspicious? Missing at the same time? What about the others?

148
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:40,580
Toka, the Yumai sisters, and Miku are all having lunch at their respective schools.

149
00:08:40,580 --> 00:08:44,580
And Natsumi and Yoshino apparently went out to play in the city together.

150
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:45,580
Gotcha.

151
00:08:45,580 --> 00:08:49,580
Well, I'd hate to make everyone worry, but we can't keep it from them forever.

152
00:08:49,580 --> 00:08:53,580
We need to find Shido fast, before all the others get home.

153
00:08:53,580 --> 00:09:04,580
Where am I?

154
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:11,580
What happened at Origami's?

155
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:19,580
It's you! Where have you been? Why were you...

156
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:23,580
Water. Bet you're a little thirsty.

157
00:09:23,580 --> 00:09:24,580
I...

158
00:09:25,580 --> 00:09:26,580
Um...

159
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:27,580
Yeah.

160
00:09:28,580 --> 00:09:29,580
Hey, stop! What are you doing?

161
00:09:29,580 --> 00:09:32,580
Yes, I want some, but only the normal way!

162
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:35,580
Thanks. Real slow...

163
00:09:44,580 --> 00:09:47,580
Look, can you help me out? Just untie me.

164
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:48,580
That I can't do.

165
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:52,580
It's true. You really joined D.E.M.

166
00:09:52,580 --> 00:09:53,580
Yes.

167
00:09:53,580 --> 00:09:56,580
And my abduction? Did Westcott order you to do this to me?

168
00:09:57,580 --> 00:10:00,580
This is all me. I brought you here of my own volition.

169
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:04,580
D.E.M. is completely unaware that I kidnapped and brought you here today.

170
00:10:05,580 --> 00:10:07,580
This is the only way to get it done.

171
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:12,580
If I was going to keep you out of it, this method held the strongest chance for success.

172
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:16,580
Hold on a sec. What do you mean, keep me out? Out of what?

173
00:10:18,580 --> 00:10:20,580
My fight is only with the spirits.

174
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:21,580
My spirits? You mean...

175
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:25,580
Of course. You know I mean them too. No exceptions.

176
00:10:25,580 --> 00:10:29,580
Wait! I thought the point was that you were after the spirit who killed your parents!

177
00:10:29,580 --> 00:10:31,580
Toka and the others had nothing to do with it!

178
00:10:31,580 --> 00:10:41,580
But spirits are all the same. If we're going to keep more humans like me from being created, then we simply cannot allow them to continue existing.

179
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:45,580
But Toka and the others don't even register as spirits!

180
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:48,580
Remember? You told me you didn't have to go after them anymore!

181
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:52,580
That was a self-defense force decision. It has nothing to do with me now.

182
00:10:57,580 --> 00:11:03,580
Think, Murakami. It's been over six months since I met Toka, and she transferred to our school.

183
00:11:03,580 --> 00:11:12,580
Man, time flies. Now the spirits you guys used to fight are a regular part of our society. Not only that, they're a part of our lives!

184
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:19,580
So how can you, you who have been here through all of it, how can you look at them and say they haven't changed?

185
00:11:20,580 --> 00:11:24,580
That it's once a spirit, always a spirit! That they're so dangerous, they need to be murdered!

186
00:11:25,580 --> 00:11:31,580
You really think I don't get it? Toka and all the others have drawn me in too, but they're spirits all the same.

187
00:11:31,580 --> 00:11:35,580
Seeing them should feed my revenge, and yet it hasn't.

188
00:11:36,580 --> 00:11:40,580
I can never forgive myself for slowly losing sight of my goal.

189
00:11:41,580 --> 00:11:45,580
Five years ago, I swore I'd get revenge for the death of my parents.

190
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:50,580
But now I live amongst my enemies. I've been so weak.

191
00:11:51,580 --> 00:11:56,580
The reason I decided to join DEM was because I realized how wrong I'd been.

192
00:11:56,580 --> 00:12:01,580
That in accepting Tokayatogami, I was betraying everything I believed.

193
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:06,580
But that's because what you believed was wrong! You know them as well as I do!

194
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:09,580
They're peaceful! All they want is to live normal lives!

195
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:14,580
No. I can't allow that. They are what they are, Shido.

196
00:12:14,580 --> 00:12:23,580
I have more to destroy than just spirits. I have to kill the girl in me who chose to take the easy way out.

197
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:29,580
I'll regain the person I was by taking the life of Tokayatogami.

198
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:33,580
Origami, wait! Please come back!

199
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:40,580
And you're okay with it, Ike? Allowing her to act on her own like this?

200
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:42,580
Doesn't matter to me.

201
00:12:42,580 --> 00:12:45,580
I'm glad she's showing some initiative.

202
00:12:46,580 --> 00:12:50,580
There's no sense dampening the enthusiasm of a young wizard, in my opinion.

203
00:12:51,580 --> 00:12:54,580
Remember, in the end, what we're after are spirits.

204
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:59,580
And the only way to measure the power of a bomb is to simply let it drop.

205
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:04,580
Be honest, aren't you a little curious about how far she'll go if given the chance?

206
00:13:04,580 --> 00:13:07,580
Very well, then. I'll do whatever I can behind the scenes.

207
00:13:08,580 --> 00:13:13,580
You're displeased, though. I can tell because your brows wrinkle right here when you have to lie.

208
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:15,580
Just kidding.

209
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:22,580
Come on, don't be mad at me. It just so happens that I have another target in mind for you this time.

210
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:24,580
We have another target?

211
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:30,580
Yes. Ratadisker. They have a certain ship that's going to get in Origami's way.

212
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:34,580
And I want you to stop it. Using Goetia, naturally.

213
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:37,580
Can't believe a tummy ache sent Shido home.

214
00:13:38,580 --> 00:13:40,580
He's too weak. We need to train him back up into shape.

215
00:13:41,580 --> 00:13:45,580
Agreed. He's turned into a wimpy wimp. Starting tomorrow, we'll make him run laps.

216
00:13:46,580 --> 00:13:48,580
I'm sure he had a good reason for leaving.

217
00:13:49,580 --> 00:13:53,580
Question. I've heard people saying that Master Origami has transferred schools for some reason.

218
00:13:54,580 --> 00:13:56,580
Do we think Shido leaving could be related to that?

219
00:13:56,580 --> 00:14:01,580
Yeah. In fact, that's exactly when he left, right after he found out about Origami.

220
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:05,580
See, I so knew that. It smelled fishy to me the whole time.

221
00:14:06,580 --> 00:14:08,580
You can smell fish? How weird. I can't smell anything.

222
00:14:09,580 --> 00:14:10,580
That's not really what I meant.

223
00:14:10,580 --> 00:14:19,580
Hey, Toka! And Kaguya! I'm Yuzuru!

224
00:14:20,580 --> 00:14:25,580
Huh? Why on earth would you choose to dodge my expression of love?

225
00:14:25,580 --> 00:14:26,580
Oh, that's what that was?

226
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:31,580
Oh, duh, of course. It's the new thing everyone's doing. Come on, bring it on in!

227
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:33,580
Don't be fooled, kinswoman.

228
00:14:33,580 --> 00:14:35,580
Warning. I definitely smell a liar.

229
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:39,580
Aha! I knew it. For starters, what the heck are you doing here anyway?

230
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:44,580
Right. Kay. I came out to visit Darling, but no one was there, so it was super boring.

231
00:14:45,580 --> 00:14:47,580
And then the house next door was empty, too.

232
00:14:48,580 --> 00:14:49,580
So you mean Shido hasn't come home yet?

233
00:14:50,580 --> 00:14:54,580
What about the Origami thing? I have a feeling that she has something to do with this.

234
00:14:54,580 --> 00:14:57,580
Agreement. I think we might actually be onto something.

235
00:14:58,580 --> 00:15:02,580
You guys! Would someone please tell me what the heck is going on? Did something happen to my darling?

236
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:05,580
Here's the deal. Right now?

237
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:07,580
Why is the spatial quake alarm going off?

238
00:15:08,580 --> 00:15:10,580
I guess we should assume another spirit showed up.

239
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:13,580
Curious. Should we all go see who this spirit is?

240
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:18,580
No, we can't do that! You know that if the alarm is sounding, that means we have to evacuate!

241
00:15:19,580 --> 00:15:20,580
I know, but Shido...

242
00:15:20,580 --> 00:15:21,580
There's no need for that.

243
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:24,580
Origami-Tobiichi? What are you doing here?

244
00:15:26,580 --> 00:15:27,580
There is no spatial quake.

245
00:15:28,580 --> 00:15:30,580
What do you mean? There must be! Just listen!

246
00:15:30,580 --> 00:15:33,580
The alarm is sounding, because I put in a request for it to do so.

247
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:36,580
Neither a spirit nor the AST are going to show up.

248
00:15:37,580 --> 00:15:40,580
But why? What would make you do something like that?

249
00:15:42,580 --> 00:15:44,580
To make it easier to kill the rest of you!

250
00:15:51,580 --> 00:16:05,580
I said, the point is to kill you! To kill all spirits!

251
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:07,580
Look at your eyes!

252
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:09,580
Oh no...

253
00:16:09,580 --> 00:16:12,580
Why have you gone back to before Origami-Tobiichi?

254
00:16:17,580 --> 00:16:18,580
So, you noticed us!

255
00:16:19,580 --> 00:16:21,580
Respect. This is our Master Origami.

256
00:16:22,580 --> 00:16:24,580
Now then, how about explaining what this is all about?

257
00:16:25,580 --> 00:16:27,580
Inquiry. Please answer our call, Master Origami.

258
00:16:28,580 --> 00:16:29,580
We have no desire to fight you today.

259
00:16:29,580 --> 00:16:30,580
I don't have to answer anything!

260
00:16:30,580 --> 00:16:32,580
I don't have to answer ANYTHING!

261
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:40,580
Send-o fun!

262
00:16:41,580 --> 00:16:43,580
Gabriel! RONDO!

263
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:44,580
No!

264
00:16:57,580 --> 00:16:59,580
Hey, you guys! Is everyone okay?

265
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:03,580
Origami isn't playing a game.

266
00:17:04,580 --> 00:17:07,580
If we don't kill her, we'll be killed.

267
00:17:09,580 --> 00:17:10,580
What are you doing, Toga?!

268
00:17:10,580 --> 00:17:13,580
Origami? Where the hell did she come from?

269
00:17:14,580 --> 00:17:16,580
Such great magical power.

270
00:17:17,580 --> 00:17:19,580
She's on a whole other level than before.

271
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:22,580
Without their full spirit armor, the others aren't safe.

272
00:17:23,580 --> 00:17:24,580
Fraxinus, full power ahead.

273
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:26,580
Let's go get them out of there.

274
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:28,580
If it gets ugly, deploy the Ectrifolium.

275
00:17:29,580 --> 00:17:30,580
Let's back them up!

276
00:17:31,580 --> 00:17:32,580
Roger!

277
00:17:33,580 --> 00:17:34,580
What was that?

278
00:17:34,580 --> 00:17:36,580
We're now under attack. Territory reduced 30%.

279
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:38,580
Enemy in our sights at 3 o'clock.

280
00:17:38,580 --> 00:17:40,580
It's... an airship!

281
00:17:40,580 --> 00:17:41,580
Are you serious?!

282
00:17:46,580 --> 00:17:47,580
Oh, great. It's DEM.

283
00:17:48,580 --> 00:17:49,580
What perfect timing.

284
00:17:50,580 --> 00:17:51,580
A transmission.

285
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:52,580
Really?

286
00:17:52,580 --> 00:17:53,580
Yes, coming from said ship.

287
00:17:53,580 --> 00:17:54,580
They're trying to reach out to the Fraxinus.

288
00:17:55,580 --> 00:17:56,580
Fine. Connect us.

289
00:17:57,580 --> 00:17:58,580
Right.

290
00:17:58,580 --> 00:17:59,580
Well, nice to meet you, I suppose.

291
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:01,580
I appreciate you accepting the transmission.

292
00:18:02,580 --> 00:18:03,580
Wait, you're Ellen Mathers.

293
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:08,580
I guess that means you've heard of me then.

294
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:10,580
It's an honor, Kotari Itsuka.

295
00:18:11,580 --> 00:18:14,580
Okay, so what business does the world's strongest wizard have with us today?

296
00:18:14,580 --> 00:18:17,580
If you want to drink tea and chat, let's do it later.

297
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:18,580
I'm a little busy right now.

298
00:18:19,580 --> 00:18:23,580
You see, a vile organization's troublesome pawn is picking a fight with our girls.

299
00:18:23,580 --> 00:18:24,580
I have two things to say.

300
00:18:25,580 --> 00:18:28,580
Number one, I'll give you up to three minutes to get out of here.

301
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:32,580
Anyone who would like to live should leave the ship without hesitation.

302
00:18:32,580 --> 00:18:37,580
You honestly believe that you could take down Fraxinus, don't you?

303
00:18:38,580 --> 00:18:41,580
All I'll say is I can't deny the possibility that it might happen.

304
00:18:42,580 --> 00:18:43,580
But seriously, Fraxinus?

305
00:18:44,580 --> 00:18:45,580
As in the tree of life.

306
00:18:46,580 --> 00:18:48,580
I assume Elliot must have chosen the name.

307
00:18:49,580 --> 00:18:52,580
Don't you think you might be underestimating Fraxinus just a little bit?

308
00:18:53,580 --> 00:18:57,580
With all due respect, perhaps you're the person who's been doing the underestimating here.

309
00:18:58,580 --> 00:19:00,580
Of my Goetia's abilities as well as my power.

310
00:19:00,580 --> 00:19:03,580
Cool. Is there anything else you want to say?

311
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:06,580
Yes. Only to the one who fled this conflict.

312
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:09,580
I have a message for you to give to Elliot.

313
00:19:10,580 --> 00:19:11,580
A message?

314
00:19:11,580 --> 00:19:15,580
Yes. Elliot. I hate you. You're a disgusting traitor.

315
00:19:16,580 --> 00:19:18,580
You turned your back on us in the promise we made.

316
00:19:19,580 --> 00:19:22,580
Prepare yourself. No matter where you hide, I swear I'm gonna find you.

317
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:24,580
I'm going to have your head.

318
00:19:26,580 --> 00:19:27,580
That's all.

319
00:19:27,580 --> 00:19:30,580
Starting now, I'll give you three minutes to evacuate.

320
00:19:30,580 --> 00:19:32,580
Please leave as quickly as you can.

321
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:38,580
Well, you heard her. We're about to be up against humanity's best, so if you want to run, you should do it now.

322
00:19:39,580 --> 00:19:44,580
Gimme a break. If I was ever gonna run away, I would have done so a dozen times before now.

323
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:48,580
Yeah. Leaving all this behind and running? How is that any different than death?

324
00:19:49,580 --> 00:19:53,580
Damn right. Who cares if it's humanity's greatest? I say we go show her what we've got.

325
00:19:54,580 --> 00:19:57,580
Say the word. I'm ready. My will is written and good to go.

326
00:19:57,580 --> 00:20:03,580
And the hard drive from my computer back home is set to a race if anything happens to me, so I'm ready. I'm in.

327
00:20:04,580 --> 00:20:07,580
But it's so hard to pass up being punished by you for running.

328
00:20:08,580 --> 00:20:10,580
Oh! Well, there you have it.

329
00:20:11,580 --> 00:20:13,580
Is that so? Such a shame.

330
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:22,580
AR-008, give three to six parallel driving force. Replenish magic power. Ready, Mistleteen. Target, DEM airship, go ATF!

331
00:20:22,580 --> 00:20:23,580
Roger!

332
00:20:23,580 --> 00:20:28,580
Coterie Itsuka, I thought you were capable of rational thought, but I guess I must have been mistaken.

333
00:20:29,580 --> 00:20:32,580
You and he may not share any blood, but you're truly Shido Itsuka's sister.

334
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:34,580
Best compliment ever.

335
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:41,580
Kanazuki, deploy Interfolium 1 through 12. It's the world's strongest wizard. Let's be prepared, just in case.

336
00:20:42,580 --> 00:20:43,580
You know, somehow I knew you'd say that.

337
00:20:45,580 --> 00:20:48,580
Let's clean things up here, then we'll go get Touka and the girls.

338
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:51,580
Replenishment complete. Mistleteen, ready to fire.

339
00:20:52,580 --> 00:20:53,580
Enemy ship Goetia hasn't moved.

340
00:20:54,580 --> 00:20:57,580
Sitting pretty for three whole minutes. She doesn't think we're serious.

341
00:20:58,580 --> 00:20:59,580
Mistleteen, fire!

342
00:21:00,580 --> 00:21:03,580
You're kidding me! What was that speed?

343
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:08,580
I think they must have thinned out the territory surrounding the ship.

344
00:21:09,580 --> 00:21:10,580
That would maximize their mobility.

345
00:21:11,580 --> 00:21:16,580
As for that driving force, best guess, they probably used territory to flick the ship aside.

346
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:18,580
Wait, you're saying that's actually possible?

347
00:21:19,580 --> 00:21:20,580
Oh, sure. Theoretically, it could be done.

348
00:21:21,580 --> 00:21:24,580
And I suppose we should expect nothing less from the Immortal Matters.

349
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:26,580
This is no time to be impressed! She's coming!

350
00:21:26,580 --> 00:21:30,580
Protect territory! Breeze for impact!

351
00:21:31,580 --> 00:21:35,580
Oh, man, you've really done it now!

352
00:21:36,580 --> 00:21:38,580
Prepare counterattack! Eat your folium to mine mode!

353
00:21:39,580 --> 00:21:40,580
Get them behind her, fast!

354
00:21:41,580 --> 00:21:42,580
Roger.

355
00:21:45,580 --> 00:21:46,580
What now?

356
00:21:46,580 --> 00:21:47,580
Another blast! Bombardment!

357
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:48,580
No!

358
00:21:48,580 --> 00:21:49,580
No!

359
00:21:58,580 --> 00:22:04,580
Help! Anyone! Is anyone out there? Anyone!

360
00:22:04,580 --> 00:22:05,580
Oh, man!

361
00:22:05,580 --> 00:22:07,580
You're the one!

362
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:08,580
No!

363
00:22:08,580 --> 00:22:09,580
No!

364
00:22:09,580 --> 00:22:10,580
No!

365
00:22:10,580 --> 00:22:11,580
No!

366
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:12,580
No!

367
00:22:12,580 --> 00:22:13,580
No!

368
00:22:14,580 --> 00:22:15,580
No!

369
00:22:15,580 --> 00:22:16,580
No!

370
00:22:16,580 --> 00:22:17,580
No!

371
00:22:18,580 --> 00:22:19,580
No!

372
00:22:20,580 --> 00:22:21,580
No!

373
00:22:21,580 --> 00:22:22,580
No!

374
00:22:22,580 --> 00:22:23,580
No!

375
00:22:23,580 --> 00:22:24,580
No!

376
00:22:24,580 --> 00:22:25,580
No!

377
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:55,560
ED

378
00:22:55,580 --> 00:23:25,560
See you next time.

379
00:23:25,580 --> 00:23:55,560
See you next time.

